  * Deleting ONE file inside the Recycle Bin was impossible (GUI Delete hit OBJECT_IDENTITY_MISMATCH 3x) -> deterministic Layer 0:
        recycle_bin_find   : Shell.Application NameSpace(10)  -> items {name, original path, backing `$R` path, size}
        recycle_bin_remove_item : permanent delete of EXACTLY ONE uniquely matched item (backing `$I`/`$R` pair; SHFileOperationW fallback)
        recycle_bin_restore_item: undelete verb (fallback: move `$R` back to the original path + drop `$I`)
    and an INDEPENDENT oracle: the item vanished from NameSpace(10), the `$R` store is gone, and SHQueryRecycleBinW dropped by exactly one.

All side effects go through a `ShellBackend` object so the whole logic is unit-testable without Windows (tests/unit/test_v17.py).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

