"""
v18.1 Unified World Model — the single trusted source of "what is true right now".

Before v18.1 the truth was scattered: UIA (`Observation.elements`), CDP (daemon/MCP), DXGI+DirectML (SoM boxes), OCR, WindowManager (HWND/PID/Z-order) and the
file-system / Shell COM probes each kept their own picture, and Layer 0 tools answered questions from private caches (stale `STALE_EPOCH`, `OBJECT_IDENTITY_MISMATCH`).

Contract
  * Perception channels and Layer-0 tools ONLY `submit()` observation snapshots (monotonic per-channel `snapshot_epoch` + timestamp).  They never answer planning questions.
  * Planner / verifier / Action-Transaction code READ through `WorldView` (a read-only facade) or an external oracle — never through a private cache.
  * Object references are IDENTITY-based (`WorldObjectRef.identity`), not position/name based; an epoch bump re-bases a frozen ref by identity (`rebase`)
    and an object that vanished or changed identity is reported, never silently replaced.
  * Cross-location target search (`search`): “删除相机文件” with no folder → Desktop / Documents / Downloads / RecycleBin inside the AUTHORIZED scope, returning real path + state
    + a classification (live_unique | live_ambiguous | bin_only | bin_ambiguous | suggest | none).

Pure Python (providers are injected) → unit-testable on any OS; production providers wrap the existing recycle_bin.ComBackend and the Win32 known-folder resolver.
